      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Ionic Compounds\n\nBinary ionic compounds contain a positive ion (cation) and a negative ion (anion). The cation is a metal in most cases, and is always written first in the formula.\n\n### Naming Rules:\n1. The cation is always named first and the anion second\n2. A cation takes its name from the element name (e.g., K⁺ is potassium)\n3. An anion is named by taking the first part of the element name and adding *-ide* (e.g., Br⁻ is bromide)\n\n### Monatomic Ions"
