      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "### Type II Binary Ionic Compounds\n\nType II compounds contain metals that can form **more than one type of cation** (e.g., Fe²⁺ and Fe³⁺).\n\nNaming: Use Roman numerals to indicate charge (e.g., iron(II) for Fe²⁺, iron(III) for Fe³⁺)\n\nAlternate naming: *-ous* suffix for lower charge, *-ic* suffix for higher charge"
